  "notes": "Batch-one channel-major InstanceNorm1d with per-channel biased variance over runtime-valid frames, affine norm weight/bias, then style (1+gamma)*norm+beta. Style projection is a separate circuit operation. Ascending FP64 statistics and FP32 affine order define this scalar numerical identity; no claim of bitwise PyTorch parity across backends. Explicit capacities and physical frame strides; padding untouched. No hidden allocation, scratch, persistent state, or backward support. Output unchanged on invalid geometry, short buffers, or nonfinite input/result. Input/output and weight aliasing unsupported. Runtime frame count may bind to a checked producer extent while memory planning uses capacity.",
